# ============================================================================
# Docker build context (repo root).
#
# Build strategy: every Python image is built with the REPOSITORY ROOT as the
# build context, because the services share a single `uv.lock` workspace. That
# makes this file — not a per-service one — the thing that decides what the
# daemon has to hash and upload.
#
# Keep:  pyproject.toml, uv.lock, services/*/pyproject.toml, services/*/README.md,
#        services/*/src/**, services/agent/alembic/**, the entrypoint script.
# Drop:  everything below — VCS, docs and assignment material, tests, runtime
#        state, caches, media.
#
# `services/*/README.md` is kept on purpose, and that is not obvious. Each service
# declares `readme = "README.md"` in its own pyproject, and hatchling reads that
# file while building the wheel — so excluding it fails the image build with
# "Readme file does not exist: README.md" *after* the dependency layer has already
# resolved, which looks like a dependency problem and is not one. It also has to be
# copied in the Dockerfile; un-ignoring it here only makes that possible.
# ============================================================================

# --- VCS -------------------------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# --- Documentation and assignment material ---------------------------------
docs
*.md
!README.md
!services/*/README.md
AGENTCORE.md
LICENSE

# --- Never ship runtime state or secrets -----------------------------------
data
.env
.env.*
secrets
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
*.pem
*.key

# --- Python caches / virtualenvs -------------------------------------------
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov
.venv
**/.venv
uv.lock.bak

# --- Tests and dev tooling (not needed inside images) ----------------------
**/tests
**/test_*.py
**/*_test.py
.pytest_cache
specs
tests

# --- The mock -------------------------------------------------------------
# `docker compose` builds it with `context: ./mock-ticketing`, and leaving it out of
# the root context keeps 30KB and a copy of the fixture out of the service images'
# hashes.
#
# Three files are re-included, and only for the single-container image at the
# repository root (`Dockerfile`), which has to start the mock itself because
# `CONTRACT.md`'s smoke test runs one container. The directory is excluded as
# `mock-ticketing/*` rather than `mock-ticketing` on purpose: Docker cannot
# re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded outright, and excluding the
# directory itself made these three lines silently do nothing — a build that failed
# later with "COPY failed: file not found", far from the ignore rule that caused it.
mock-ticketing/*
!mock-ticketing/app.py
!mock-ticketing/seed.py
!mock-ticketing/requirements.txt

# --- Editor / OS noise -----------------------------------------------------
.idea
.vscode
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.log
